# The refine helper uses the `claude` CLI (your Claude Code / Anthropic
# subscription) — there is NO API key to set. Just make sure you're logged in:
# run `claude` once in a terminal if it asks you to authenticate.
#
# Everything below is OPTIONAL. Copy to .env only if you want to override a default.

# Which model the CLI uses for rewrites (any alias the claude CLI accepts).
# REFINE_MODEL=haiku

# Port the helper listens on. If you change it, also update HELPER in extension/background.js.
# REFINE_PORT=8730

# Path to the claude binary, if it isn't on PATH.
# CLAUDE_BIN=claude

# ── Resume tailoring (opt-in: pass --tailor, or TAILOR=1) ───────────────────
# There is still NO API key. Tailoring uses the same `claude` CLI as the refine
# helper, i.e. your existing Claude Code subscription auth.
#
# Or hand the model work to another host: an endpoint taking {base, jobDescription}
# and returning {tailored}. The headless runner has no interactive claude login, so
# this is how it tailors.
# APPLY_AGENT_TAILOR_ENDPOINT=https://orchestrator.example/tailor
# APPLY_AGENT_SERVICE_TOKEN=<bearer token for that endpoint>
#
# Which model the claude CLI uses for tailoring (default: sonnet).
# APPLY_AGENT_TAILOR_MODEL=sonnet
#
# How long a RENDERED tailored PDF is kept before `apply-agent resume gc` deletes it.
# The markdown source it came from is kept forever and regenerates the PDF on demand.
# APPLY_AGENT_RESUME_RENDER_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# ── Orchestrator endpoints (both private-network-only, both bearer-authenticated) ─
# Some work needs a model or a mailbox the runner should not hold credentials for.
# The orchestrator host has both, so the runner stores ONE secret instead of a model
# key and mail credentials.
#
# FALLBACK ONLY. src/util/email-code.js reads the code from Gmail in the same warm
# browser session that is filling the form — no password, no IMAP, and better for
# anti-bot reasons than an out-of-band relay. This endpoint is called only after that
# returns null, and every fallback is recorded as friction so a Gmail DOM change
# becomes visible instead of quietly degrading into abandoned applications.
# APPLY_AGENT_EMAIL_CODE_ENDPOINT=https://orchestrator.example/email-code
#
# Timeouts and the cooldown breaker. Short by design: the orchestrator being down must
# reduce a run's quality, never stall it or strand a browser mid-application.
# APPLY_AGENT_EMAIL_CODE_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
# APPLY_AGENT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
# APPLY_AGENT_ENDPOINT_COOLDOWN_MS=60000
#
# Check both endpoints before a run: npm run doctor
